{"title":"2004 IMO Problems/Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find all <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Polynomial\" title=\"Polynomial\">polynomials</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> with real coefficients such that for all reals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/b/a5b29b358e825defa3e11b7d903d43ec31e5909a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b,c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/3/123bf434194420af32656c7d781a101c96db2254.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab + bc + ca = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"127\" height=\"14\" /> we have the following relations\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/c/ffc10b907c24b5bb71310bf84a608863d9abdcc3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(a - b) + f(b - c) + f(c - a) = 2f(a + b + c).\\]\" width=\"368\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>From <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/6/626229304da6c19648940d39d8168809792a5867.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=c=0$\" width=\"72\" height=\"12\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/1/1b12e0aae5c83d44d98697ed3efe5730b3e2bbce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(a) + f(-a) = 2f(a) \\Longrightarrow f(a) = f(-a)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"318\" height=\"18\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> is even, and all the degrees all of its terms are even. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/f/6ffd3483e7f168b19bd68bb52b8df72541193deb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{deg}\\, f(x) = n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"98\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/a/e7a886e4242b1a43935b401e3048dabf7d59829a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,b,c) = (6x, 3x, -2x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"181\" height=\"18\" />*; then we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/d/21d842d5fad4f0d7f9b8dd3c12aa43aa7a6d5082.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(3x) + f(5x) + f(8x) = 2f(7x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"254\" height=\"18\" />. Comparing lead coefficients, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/d/90d002be665bd07594fd00879e118985a16b8632.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3^n + 5^n + 8^n = 2 \\cdot 7^n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"162\" height=\"14\" />, which cannot be true for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/e/a1e903a5a7c9e6f17b32bf920da41cdb640afbd7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\ge 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"46\" height=\"16\" />. Hence, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/f/bafa28f6ebf0b87ee8c45a53e97f32c21c7dccb2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) = c_1 x^4 + c_2 x^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"147\" height=\"19\" />. We can easily verify by expanding that all such polynomials work. \n</p>\n<ul><li><font style=\"font-size:85%\">The substitution arises from writing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/1/f91da3d93cebb398b6264eb955f365540b149e55.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = \\frac{-bc}{b+c}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"74\" height=\"39\" />.</font></li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/6/ca658ac249cf7464e4ef635204605971050ac097.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = (1 - \\sqrt {3})x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"113\" height=\"21\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/8/cc88f3823c803b02195a423b5ca1669e00407fe5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = x$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/5/6d51c484f5faad094c938d5dd653d6e6f48905d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c = (1 + \\sqrt {3})x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"111\" height=\"21\" />.  Then it is easy to check that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/3/123bf434194420af32656c7d781a101c96db2254.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab + bc + ca = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"127\" height=\"14\" />, so\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/7/297d4af94fbfbf0998639120538208a0e1b94911.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[P( - \\sqrt {3}x) + P( - \\sqrt {3}x) + P(2 \\sqrt {3} x) = 2P(3x)\\]\" width=\"350\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />.  Hence, for the coefficient of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/7/8c72f3acf1f7744cfe76edaf47e45d62432cf28b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^n$\" width=\"18\" height=\"12\" /> to be nonzero, we must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/4/39433254c5fa8858ae88939876417c5321cd9ab3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2( - \\sqrt {3})^n + (2 \\sqrt {3})^n = 2 \\cdot 3^n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"213\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p>This does not hold for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/6/c766f9fce6070981e62f805a7cf7294baed4498e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />, and if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is odd and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/1/8f1e2533d6abdb11a9a1626c0240fab1a9200fc6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\ge 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />, then the LHS is irrational and the RHS is a positive integer, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> must be even.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/e/ffe388d3a177b46bbb5eb8b642b423091e6ab74f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 2m$\" width=\"59\" height=\"12\" />.  Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/8/7484777aefb41f55faa9d9c01b75a4647dbc054b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\cdot 3^m + 12^m = 2 \\cdot 3^{2m}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"170\" height=\"16\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/6/c56ac827fd7cf6716ec5bdab78a4fb930d7ee92b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 + 4^m = 2 \\cdot 3^m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"120\" height=\"14\" />.  This holds for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/b/73baad1d05e4bc4d4067fd6dfcc164e339bf981a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"48\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/5/865dd25261a2f76b4036ca6b566e0d94c0ffd612.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f5c2a60de0fa94006b35a1f0b609c17b66b8b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4/3)^3 = 64/27 &gt; 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"151\" height=\"19\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/d/7edb5c50034dfe7b5935a978f38b480e267c1722.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 + 4^m &gt; 4^m &gt; 2 \\cdot 3^m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"166\" height=\"14\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/c/ebce24f0635031abe14eebf583fff15b054ea587.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m \\ge 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"48\" height=\"15\" />.  Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/f/6efaaf74e576202fad965134bc49c6a34aac4c30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> must be of the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/1/d11e92824bf33c1ecc8cf1ad95e9bc7a78d65d42.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_2 x^2 + a_4 x^4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"91\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li>&lt;url&gt;viewtopic.php?p=99448#99448 AoPS/MathLinks discussion&lt;/url&gt;</li></ul>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_IMO\" title=\"2004 IMO\">2004 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_IMO_Problems\" title=\"2004 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2004 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2004 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2004 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2004 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2004 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2004 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2004 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017090117\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.025 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.039 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 223/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 894/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 44/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 6606/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.858      1 Template:IMO_box\n100.00%    6.858      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:7411:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017090117 and revision id 204508. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}